{"caller": "claude", "commit": "e67e5007c715ea7e15e75ba43e31d74ad61e6a06", "date": "2026-10-06T07:52:17+00:00", "exit": 0, "files": ["AGENTS.md", "docs/review-checklist.md", "justfile", "plans/20261006-review-process.status.md", "plans/20261006-review-process.task.md", "tests/test_review.py", "tests/test_review_log.py", "tests/test_review_stats.py", "tools/review.py", "tools/review_log.py", "tools/review_select.py", "tools/review_stats.py"], "findings": [{"id": "20261006T075217Z-e67e5007#1", "line": 34, "path": "tools/review_stats.py", "rule": "R1", "severity": "should", "text": "`RuleStats.outcomes` repeats the allowed outcomes as a literal inside the counting mechanism. Fix: construct the counters from the documented `OUTCOMES` definition."}, {"id": "20261006T075217Z-e67e5007#2", "line": 99, "path": "tools/review_log.py", "rule": "R9", "severity": "should", "text": "The docstrings for `log_path`, `append`, and `read` describe their results or operations but omit their purpose. Fix: explain the test override and how persistence supports review history."}, {"id": "20261006T075217Z-e67e5007#3", "line": 136, "path": "tools/review_log.py", "rule": "R10", "severity": "should", "text": "The unknown-finding error gives no corrective action. Fix: tell the user to copy a finding ID printed by `just review` and select the corresponding log."}, {"id": "20261006T075217Z-e67e5007#4", "line": 113, "path": "tools/review.py", "rule": "R11", "severity": "should", "text": "Logging failed and malformed reviews is new behavior without a test that verifies those records are written. Fix: add tests that exercise reviewer failure and malformed output and assert the resulting failure records."}], "id": "20261006T075217Z-e67e5007", "kind": "review", "reviewer": "codex", "revision": "@-", "rules": {"R1": "62d446279093", "R10": "638d8cbd1df8", "R11": "5de19cdbbbc1", "R12": "99f66579f467", "R13": "da0926dafb88", "R2": "e5e78fb2a52a", "R3": "4f9188eadd60", "R4": "ea7ca17539eb", "R5": "b8613a2d