{"caller": "codex", "commit": "f1617c4a12ac1b1a5de19892986c6302be302f97", "date": "2026-10-06T08:46:50+00:00", "exit": 0, "files": ["plans/20261006-optional-upstream-catalog.status.md", "tests/conformance_catalog_test.py", "tests/test_conformance_catalog_environment.py"], "findings": [{"id": "20261006T084650Z-f1617c4a#1", "line": 23, "path": "tests/conformance_catalog_test.py", "rule": "R10", "severity": "should", "text": "When `CONFORMANCE_UPSTREAM` is set to an empty string, `Path('')` becomes `.`, so the message says \"has no test directory: .\" and does not tell the user that the variable is empty. If the current directory happens to contain a `test` directory, the empty value is accepted with no error. Fix: check for an empty value before the path check and fail with a message that says the variable is set but empty and must point to the pinned SQLite source archive."}], "id": "20261006T084650Z-f1617c4a", "kind": "review", "reviewer": "claude", "revision": "f1617c4a", "rules": {"R1": "62d446279093", "R10": "638d8cbd1df8", "R11": "5de19cdbbbc1", "R12": "99f66579f467", "R13": "da0926dafb88", "R2": "e5e78fb2a52a", "R3": "4f9188eadd60", "R4": "ea7ca17539eb", "R5": "b8613a2d693b", "R6": "5600dce59aef", "R7": "0b68df581c57", "R8": "b4168359c60d", "R9": "5a69196344d0"}, "well_formed": true}
